WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:02.060
- Hey guys, Dr. Mike Varshavski here.

00:00:02.060 --> 00:00:04.640
Welcome to another episode
of the Wednesday Checkup.

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:07.470
In the past, I made a
COVID-19 fact checking video

00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:11.160
on politicians, media,
even conspiracy theorists.

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:13.430
But today, I wanna focus
on President Trump.

00:00:13.430 --> 00:00:14.670
And the reason I'm doing this

00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:17.080
is not because of a political motivation,

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:19.530
but simply because he's the
leader of the United States,

00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:21.590
he's in charge of making
a lot of the decisions

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:23.900
that affect you and I
in our day-to-day lives;

00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:25.890
funding, testing, decisions

00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:27.890
about potential treatments
and vaccinations.

00:00:27.890 --> 00:00:29.500
And I think it's important to be critical

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:32.050
of our leaders so that we
can hold them accountable

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:33.850
to the statements and
the decisions they make.

00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:35.520
I've been following the media reports

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:38.050
very closely surrounding COVID-19.

00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:39.430
There's been heavy reporting

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:42.070
both in the United States and outside

00:00:42.070 --> 00:00:44.500
talking about how America has failed

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:46.120
in the COVID-19 pandemic.

00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:47.920
And while there's certainly truth to that,

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:48.920
we need to be fair.

00:00:48.920 --> 00:00:51.140
No one can be truly
prepared for a pandemic,

00:00:51.140 --> 00:00:52.190
we need to put that out there.

00:00:52.190 --> 00:00:54.930
Also, hindsight is 20/20 and everyone

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:56.960
loves to play Monday morning quarterback.

00:00:56.960 --> 00:00:59.470
That being said, President Trump has made

00:00:59.470 --> 00:01:01.120
several inaccurate statements

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:02.640
that I'm gonna cover here today.

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:04.910
As a leader, you wanna project confidence,

00:01:04.910 --> 00:01:07.740
you wanna project being
alert, not anxious.

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:10.610
However, that doesn't
mean we should downplay

00:01:10.610 --> 00:01:12.400
truly serious issues.

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:14.210
And throughout this pandemic,

00:01:14.210 --> 00:01:16.790
the messaging from President
Trump has been this.

00:01:16.790 --> 00:01:18.403
- I think that's a problem
that's gonna go away.

00:01:18.403 --> 00:01:20.000
It's going to disappear.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:20.833
It will go away.

00:01:20.833 --> 00:01:21.868
It will go away.

00:01:21.868 --> 00:01:22.701
It's gonna go away.

00:01:22.701 --> 00:01:23.534
You know it is going away.

00:01:23.534 --> 00:01:25.323
It is going away, this is gonna go away.

00:01:25.323 --> 00:01:26.300
It's gonna go, it's gonna leave.

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:29.150
- COVID-19 is gonna go away

00:01:29.150 --> 00:01:32.010
won't be a problem for the rest our lives,

00:01:32.010 --> 00:01:35.020
but to continually say this
in the midst of pandemic

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:38.330
when hundreds of thousands
of lives are being lost,

00:01:38.330 --> 00:01:40.100
millions of people are getting infected,

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:43.450
it's just not an accurate
representation of what's going on.

00:01:43.450 --> 00:01:45.340
You're talking points have to change

00:01:45.340 --> 00:01:46.580
when you get new numbers in.

00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:49.950
When I tell you at home to
not look at numbers everyday,

00:01:49.950 --> 00:01:51.810
that's because I don't
want you becoming anxious

00:01:51.810 --> 00:01:53.870
over each of these numbers going up.

00:01:53.870 --> 00:01:55.440
But as the President of United States,

00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:56.780
a person who's in charge of making

00:01:56.780 --> 00:01:58.530
really important day-to-day decisions,

00:01:58.530 --> 00:02:00.300
you have to be looking at these numbers

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:02.600
and seeing that this
problem isn't going away.

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:04.550
In fact, I think where
President Trump showed

00:02:04.550 --> 00:02:06.940
the least amount of
accuracy in his speaking

00:02:06.940 --> 00:02:09.960
was on the day that I published
my video two weeks ago.

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:11.780
COVID cases are spiking,

00:02:11.780 --> 00:02:15.800
people are dying, and the
second wave isn't even here yet.

00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:18.260
And here's what President
Trump said that same day.

00:02:18.260 --> 00:02:19.210
- It's dying out.

00:02:19.210 --> 00:02:21.460
It's fading away, it's going to fade away.

00:02:21.460 --> 00:02:23.170
- Fast forward now to two weeks later,

00:02:23.170 --> 00:02:24.570
the problem hasn't gone away.

00:02:24.570 --> 00:02:26.090
It's actually gotten so bad

00:02:26.090 --> 00:02:29.500
that the peak of COVID-19 is
higher than it was in April.

00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:31.300
We have to take this virus seriously.

00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:32.410
Because if we don't,

00:02:32.410 --> 00:02:33.430
you know what happens?

00:02:33.430 --> 00:02:34.700
It starts spiking again.

00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:37.330
Exactly as it is happening right now.

00:02:37.330 --> 00:02:38.950
I've consistently preach

00:02:38.950 --> 00:02:41.050
that we need personal responsibility.

00:02:41.050 --> 00:02:43.470
A serious level of responsibility

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:46.130
in order to stop or at
least slow down this virus,

00:02:46.130 --> 00:02:48.110
meaning that we need to
socially distance ourselves,

00:02:48.110 --> 00:02:50.200
we need to wear masks, wash our hands.

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:52.580
That being said, there is still something

00:02:52.580 --> 00:02:54.170
that our government needs to do

00:02:54.170 --> 00:02:55.740
and that's testing.

00:02:55.740 --> 00:02:57.250
That's their responsibility.

00:02:57.250 --> 00:02:59.320
We need to have testing
supplies available,

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:00.730
and we need to make it out of price

00:03:00.730 --> 00:03:02.400
that's affordable to everybody.

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:05.290
In fact, it probably should
be covered by our government,

00:03:05.290 --> 00:03:06.760
like it is in many other countries.

00:03:06.760 --> 00:03:08.600
President Trump is going on stage

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:09.820
and saying things like this.

00:03:09.820 --> 00:03:14.100
- We've tested now 25 million people.

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:15.460
Here's the bad part.

00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:18.630
When you test the, when you
do testing to that extent,

00:03:18.630 --> 00:03:19.750
you're gonna find more people,

00:03:19.750 --> 00:03:21.630
you're gonna find more cases.

00:03:21.630 --> 00:03:22.877
So I said to my people,

00:03:22.877 --> 00:03:25.130
"Slow the testing down, please!"

00:03:25.130 --> 00:03:28.510
- I can't imagine anyone at the CDC

00:03:28.510 --> 00:03:30.980
or any respectable medical agency

00:03:30.980 --> 00:03:32.160
hearing our president saying

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:34.820
we should slow down testing
and taking him seriously.

00:03:34.820 --> 00:03:36.200
Here's what his staff has said.

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:38.020
- It was a comment that he made in jest,

00:03:38.020 --> 00:03:40.310
it's a comment that he made in passing."

00:03:40.310 --> 00:03:42.350
- It was tongue-in-cheek, come on now.

00:03:42.350 --> 00:03:43.720
Come on now, that was tongue-in-cheek.

00:03:43.720 --> 00:03:45.940
- I understand that there's
not much of a sense of humor

00:03:45.940 --> 00:03:48.230
at CNN center, but the
president was joking.

00:03:48.230 --> 00:03:51.940
- So let's say he's joking, why?

00:03:51.940 --> 00:03:53.410
You're the leader of our nation.

00:03:53.410 --> 00:03:55.840
We're looking to you for information.

00:03:55.840 --> 00:03:57.490
A lot of people trust you.

00:03:57.490 --> 00:04:00.310
And then after his staff
says it was a joke,

00:04:00.310 --> 00:04:01.460
President Trump says this.

00:04:01.460 --> 00:04:03.390
- [Interviewer] At that
rally when you said

00:04:03.390 --> 00:04:05.880
you asked your people
to slow down testing,

00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:08.200
were you just kidding
or do you have a plan

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:09.180
to slow down testing?

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:10.220
- I don't kid.

00:04:10.220 --> 00:04:11.053
Let me just tell you.

00:04:11.053 --> 00:04:12.010
Let me make it clear.

00:04:12.010 --> 00:04:13.610
- So he's not kidding.

00:04:13.610 --> 00:04:16.017
On top of it, when President Trump says,

00:04:16.017 --> 00:04:18.870
"The numbers are going up
because we're testing more,"

00:04:18.870 --> 00:04:19.930
that is a fallacy.

00:04:19.930 --> 00:04:21.370
We are catching more cases.

00:04:21.370 --> 00:04:22.203
But at the same time,

00:04:22.203 --> 00:04:23.450
we're having more and more sick people

00:04:23.450 --> 00:04:24.830
and virus transmission.

00:04:24.830 --> 00:04:27.450
That is showed by increased
hospitalization rate

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:29.240
and an increased positivity rate

00:04:29.240 --> 00:04:30.740
on the people who we are testing.

00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:33.280
And in fact, President
Trump leads us to believe

00:04:33.280 --> 00:04:35.890
that we have the biggest
testing capacity in the world.

00:04:35.890 --> 00:04:39.050
We're eighth in per-capita
testing in the world.

00:04:39.050 --> 00:04:41.540
Not number one, not number two, eight.

00:04:41.540 --> 00:04:43.240
So we could do a better job.

00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:45.750
And we certainly shouldn't
start slowing things down now

00:04:45.750 --> 00:04:47.660
when the virus is at its
highest peak it has been.

00:04:47.660 --> 00:04:49.570
Let's chat mortality rates.

00:04:49.570 --> 00:04:51.967
Just last week, President Trump tweeted,

00:04:51.967 --> 00:04:54.330
"Coronavirus deaths are way down.

00:04:54.330 --> 00:04:57.360
Mortality rate is one of
the lowest in the world."

00:04:57.360 --> 00:04:58.690
We aren't the lowest in the world.

00:04:58.690 --> 00:05:00.380
We're somewhere in the mid-30s.

00:05:00.380 --> 00:05:02.830
So we are not the best in
the world by any means.

00:05:02.830 --> 00:05:04.620
I'm not even a huge fan of comparing

00:05:04.620 --> 00:05:05.680
all of these numbers.

00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:07.110
There's many countries in the world

00:05:07.110 --> 00:05:08.390
that don't do a great job

00:05:08.390 --> 00:05:12.600
in keeping exact deaths,
rates, certificates of death.

00:05:12.600 --> 00:05:14.910
There's all sorts of
biases that come into play,

00:05:14.910 --> 00:05:16.880
but that being said, we're
not number one anyway.

00:05:16.880 --> 00:05:19.760
Coronavirus deaths, are they way down?

00:05:19.760 --> 00:05:23.540
Well, they're down and we kind
of expect them to come up.

00:05:23.540 --> 00:05:24.530
The reason I'm saying this

00:05:24.530 --> 00:05:26.400
is 'cause we see the cases going up,

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:27.890
but the deaths aren't going up.

00:05:27.890 --> 00:05:30.600
So President Trump is taking
this as a positive sign.

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:33.470
But I approach that with a
little bit of skepticism.

00:05:33.470 --> 00:05:34.940
Usually, there's a lag time

00:05:34.940 --> 00:05:37.520
between COVID-19 initial infection

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:39.920
and then deaths because it takes time

00:05:39.920 --> 00:05:41.490
to succumb to the virus,

00:05:41.490 --> 00:05:43.710
and then it takes time
to report that death.

00:05:43.710 --> 00:05:45.820
Second, we're seeing a lot of young folks

00:05:45.820 --> 00:05:46.940
get infected with this virus,

00:05:46.940 --> 00:05:49.640
and generally speaking they
have a lower mortality rate

00:05:49.640 --> 00:05:52.370
than the people who are
over the age of 50 or 60.

00:05:52.370 --> 00:05:53.840
And then the final point is,

00:05:53.840 --> 00:05:55.630
we have some treatments out there.

00:05:55.630 --> 00:05:58.540
Remdesivir, dexamethasone, both treatments

00:05:58.540 --> 00:06:00.420
that are being used in the severely ill,

00:06:00.420 --> 00:06:02.990
hoping to prevent or
lower the chance of death.

00:06:02.990 --> 00:06:05.140
We also learned how to
manage ventilators better.

00:06:05.140 --> 00:06:06.300
In the beginning of this pandemic,

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:07.430
this was a novel virus.

00:06:07.430 --> 00:06:09.500
We were learning, we were
trying different settings.

00:06:09.500 --> 00:06:11.620
As we've established better parameters,

00:06:11.620 --> 00:06:14.440
we've done better at taking
care of patients with COVID-19.

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:16.120
I hope that President Trump is right

00:06:16.120 --> 00:06:18.510
and that the deaths do
continue trending downward,

00:06:18.510 --> 00:06:20.490
but base on the information
we have at hand,

00:06:20.490 --> 00:06:22.980
I don't think we can make
that prediction just yet.

00:06:22.980 --> 00:06:24.463
- Coronavirus, right?

00:06:25.686 --> 00:06:26.910
(crowd yelling)

00:06:26.910 --> 00:06:28.466
Kung flu, yeah?

00:06:28.466 --> 00:06:29.299
(crowd cheering)

00:06:29.299 --> 00:06:30.870
- What's the purpose
of calling it kung flu?

00:06:30.870 --> 00:06:33.000
You're not a standup comedian.

00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:35.110
I want to laugh at ourselves,

00:06:35.110 --> 00:06:36.580
at our problems, at our pain,

00:06:36.580 --> 00:06:37.730
I believe it's therapeutic,

00:06:37.730 --> 00:06:39.850
but not right now.

00:06:39.850 --> 00:06:41.900
Not when the country is polarized

00:06:41.900 --> 00:06:43.670
we need to bring together.

00:06:43.670 --> 00:06:45.730
This isn't effective at anything

00:06:45.730 --> 00:06:47.691
except rallying his base.

00:06:47.691 --> 00:06:51.591
- Covid, COVID-19, covid,
I said what's the 19?

00:06:51.591 --> 00:06:53.991
COVID-19, some people
can't explain what the 19.

00:06:55.109 --> 00:06:56.980
COVID-19, I said, "That's an odd name."

00:06:56.980 --> 00:06:59.724
- There's nothing odd about COVID-19.

00:06:59.724 --> 00:07:02.390
19 stands for the year
that it was found, 2019.

00:07:02.390 --> 00:07:05.890
It's almost as if President
Trump wants to demean this virus

00:07:05.890 --> 00:07:08.860
so much that it's not as powerful

00:07:08.860 --> 00:07:11.540
taking the power away from his campaign.

00:07:11.540 --> 00:07:14.190
- But I get a lot of tremendously

00:07:14.190 --> 00:07:16.440
positive news on the hydroxy.

00:07:16.440 --> 00:07:18.420
- I've talked about hydroxychloroquine

00:07:18.420 --> 00:07:21.190
many times on this
channel and on television.

00:07:21.190 --> 00:07:22.920
It really bothered me when President Trump

00:07:22.920 --> 00:07:24.070
called it a game changer

00:07:24.070 --> 00:07:27.740
without having any real good
evidence to back that up.

00:07:27.740 --> 00:07:30.420
And because of that, patients
took it unnecessarily,

00:07:30.420 --> 00:07:32.660
potentially had negative
effect as a result.

00:07:32.660 --> 00:07:34.230
And really saw limited benefit.

00:07:34.230 --> 00:07:36.290
- You know the expression I've used, John?

00:07:36.290 --> 00:07:37.910
What do you have to lose?

00:07:37.910 --> 00:07:39.460
Okay, what do you have to lose?

00:07:40.360 --> 00:07:42.010
- Your life.

00:07:42.010 --> 00:07:45.120
Medications, even ones that have a known

00:07:45.120 --> 00:07:48.000
safety profile have side effects.

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:50.970
I've had many patients contact me

00:07:50.970 --> 00:07:52.930
from home when they were quite sick

00:07:52.930 --> 00:07:54.970
and said they didn't
wanna go to the hospital,

00:07:54.970 --> 00:07:57.460
they just wanted me to
prescribe hydroxychloroquine

00:07:57.460 --> 00:07:59.800
because they saw President
Trump make statements like this.

00:07:59.800 --> 00:08:01.460
And it took a lot of counseling

00:08:01.460 --> 00:08:03.490
to explain what they could lose.

00:08:03.490 --> 00:08:05.780
They can get arrhythmia,
they can lose their lives

00:08:05.780 --> 00:08:07.240
as a result of this arrhythmia

00:08:07.240 --> 00:08:08.840
because they're taking this medication

00:08:08.840 --> 00:08:10.380
without getting an EKG first.

00:08:10.380 --> 00:08:12.150
There's a lot of reasons why doctors

00:08:12.150 --> 00:08:14.010
don't prescribe medications willy-nilly

00:08:14.010 --> 00:08:16.180
and one of them is side effects.

00:08:16.180 --> 00:08:18.180
That's probably the most
important one of them all.

00:08:18.180 --> 00:08:20.130
Let's talk second wave.

00:08:20.130 --> 00:08:21.780
It's at the tip of everyone's tongue,

00:08:21.780 --> 00:08:23.180
we're all worried about it,

00:08:23.180 --> 00:08:24.990
what's the deal with the second wave?

00:08:24.990 --> 00:08:26.550
Here's what our politicians think.

00:08:26.550 --> 00:08:28.310
- There is no second wave coming.

00:08:28.310 --> 00:08:32.020
It's just hot spots
they send in CDC teams.

00:08:32.020 --> 00:08:33.720
We've got the testing procedures,

00:08:33.720 --> 00:08:35.100
we've got the diagnostics,

00:08:35.100 --> 00:08:36.770
we've got the PPE,

00:08:36.770 --> 00:08:40.610
and so I really think it's
a pretty good situation.

00:08:40.610 --> 00:08:43.137
- Only Larry Kudlow can
go on television say,

00:08:43.137 --> 00:08:45.050
"It's a pretty good situation,"

00:08:45.050 --> 00:08:46.670
when we're hitting the biggest peak

00:08:46.670 --> 00:08:48.830
we've had with COVID-19 cases.

00:08:48.830 --> 00:08:50.720
It just doesn't make sense to me.

00:08:50.720 --> 00:08:52.100
You're lying to yourself.

00:08:52.100 --> 00:08:53.710
And in fact that's not the first time

00:08:53.710 --> 00:08:55.510
Larry Kudlow has went on TV

00:08:55.510 --> 00:08:57.640
and said something quite inaccurate.

00:08:57.640 --> 00:08:59.600
- We have contained this.

00:08:59.600 --> 00:09:02.690
I won't say air-tight, but
pretty close to air-tight.

00:09:02.690 --> 00:09:04.030
- No, Larry Kudlow.

00:09:04.030 --> 00:09:07.470
It's July and we still
have not contained this.

00:09:07.470 --> 00:09:09.530
We're still experiencing all time highs,

00:09:09.530 --> 00:09:11.320
despite the European Union

00:09:11.320 --> 00:09:13.920
having a very low number of cases.

00:09:13.920 --> 00:09:15.640
So we're clearly doing something wrong

00:09:15.640 --> 00:09:17.830
and we have to be forthcoming
and honest about it.

00:09:17.830 --> 00:09:20.360
But Larry Kudlow did say
one thing accurately.

00:09:20.360 --> 00:09:21.730
There is no second wave.

00:09:21.730 --> 00:09:24.430
But that's only because we
haven't even left the first wave.

00:09:24.430 --> 00:09:26.810
The cases of COVID-19
spiked in the United States

00:09:26.810 --> 00:09:28.710
we were happy they didn't spike that high.

00:09:28.710 --> 00:09:30.400
We did all the social distancing,

00:09:30.400 --> 00:09:31.880
and then we relaxed everything

00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:33.010
and what do you know?

00:09:33.010 --> 00:09:34.750
It just continues going right back up.

00:09:34.750 --> 00:09:37.230
How has Larry Kudlow and President Trump

00:09:37.230 --> 00:09:39.110
not changed their talking points

00:09:39.110 --> 00:09:40.700
when the numbers are clearly going up.

00:09:40.700 --> 00:09:43.250
We shouldn't be using COVID-19

00:09:43.250 --> 00:09:45.920
as a chess piece in a political game.

00:09:45.920 --> 00:09:48.640
We need to be looking at
these numbers honestly,

00:09:48.640 --> 00:09:51.370
we need to be giving accurate
information to the public,

00:09:51.370 --> 00:09:54.000
so they can make the best
decisions and actions

00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:55.650
for themselves and their families.

00:09:55.650 --> 00:09:58.540
Until we can put our
political nonsense aside,

00:09:58.540 --> 00:10:00.470
we will not get anywhere.

00:10:00.470 --> 00:10:03.140
Because the general public is confused.

00:10:03.140 --> 00:10:05.700
I watch media, I'm confused.

00:10:05.700 --> 00:10:07.720
I have to read dense research

00:10:07.720 --> 00:10:09.960
in order to figure out what's going on.

00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:12.530
The average person cannot do that,

00:10:12.530 --> 00:10:13.530
therefore they're led astray.

00:10:13.530 --> 00:10:18.020
We need a non-bias approach to COVID-19.

00:10:18.020 --> 00:10:19.570
Let's stop playing the blame game

00:10:19.570 --> 00:10:21.690
and just give the accurate information

00:10:21.690 --> 00:10:25.270
of what's going on and
accurate non-political snapshot

00:10:25.270 --> 00:10:28.070
as well as some guidelines
that aren't political as well.

00:10:28.070 --> 00:10:30.700
Covering your face in public
to protect a community

00:10:30.700 --> 00:10:32.310
is not a political statement.

00:10:32.310 --> 00:10:35.990
You do not need to put on a
"Make America Great Again" hat

00:10:35.990 --> 00:10:38.030
and put the mask over your eyes

00:10:38.030 --> 00:10:39.430
to show how cool you are.

00:10:39.430 --> 00:10:40.540
And at the same time,

00:10:40.540 --> 00:10:42.660
if you see someone not wearing a mask,

00:10:42.660 --> 00:10:45.580
yelling at them won't
help the situation either.

00:10:45.580 --> 00:10:47.900
Explaining to them why the mask

00:10:47.900 --> 00:10:49.800
is important could be a step,

00:10:49.800 --> 00:10:52.470
but yelling at them is only
gonna make the problem worse

00:10:52.470 --> 00:10:55.130
and the polarization
continue to trend upwards.

00:10:55.130 --> 00:10:56.970
We need to do this smartly,

00:10:56.970 --> 00:10:59.810
non-politically, and in a scientific way.

00:10:59.810 --> 00:11:03.000
All in all, I have this final
message for President Trump.

00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:05.070
You are the leader of the United States.

00:11:05.070 --> 00:11:07.330
The country that I call home

00:11:07.330 --> 00:11:09.470
that my family escaped to from Russia.

00:11:09.470 --> 00:11:12.970
Your responsibility to
people to be honest,

00:11:12.970 --> 00:11:15.630
to be forthcoming with information

00:11:15.630 --> 00:11:17.380
that we can use to protect ourselves

00:11:17.380 --> 00:11:18.740
and our family members.

00:11:18.740 --> 00:11:23.670
Please avoid sarcastic,
jokey, or even mean rhetoric

00:11:23.670 --> 00:11:25.400
when talking about COVID-19.

00:11:25.400 --> 00:11:27.780
It creates confusion and confusion

00:11:27.780 --> 00:11:31.460
in the midst of a pandemic
costs people their lives.

00:11:31.460 --> 00:11:33.510
I'm a front line healthcare worker.

00:11:33.510 --> 00:11:36.340
The last thing I wanna see
is my patients get sick

00:11:36.340 --> 00:11:38.010
or even my colleagues get sick.

00:11:38.010 --> 00:11:40.470
You have the ability to
bring this nation together.

00:11:40.470 --> 00:11:42.620
But you have to do that by starting

00:11:42.620 --> 00:11:46.853
to be honest, forthcoming,
and unifying in your message.

